wer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a6d5900-d582-5696-bf23-419f8018557a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331264} {:answer/id #uuid "69ef443a-49a1-5e5f-8a20-4f1e90e21c83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331265} {:answer/id #uuid "265c5224-c71e-500e-9413-c8bb93873f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331266} {:answer/id #uuid "aa93b2dd-d0f6-58e7-b06e-2876a03d82bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331267} {:answer/id #uuid "2c5d92b5-08b3-5380-b46d-c958625a0ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69ef443a-49a1-5e5f-8a20-4f1e90e21c83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331265} :answer-field/id #uuid "c82dc270-0c50-53e3-92cb-3ba117c45cfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3333941c-b382-595a-913e-d99dd113743a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129666" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,1]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/78af77d697ea292385e2bd2570c8185c728f57cc70c3edcc25ecccd0e84780e8.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles II and III do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle I cover the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "100ab73e-3dad-5b15-9da2-d244c67bcc9b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7452e190-5efb-5f88-b12b-2ed2926bb308" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331271} {:answer/id #uuid "5a3af402-4519-56a2-8e33-e68188ec2762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331272} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e2551c-92ac-57f8-815e-671ca231739f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331273} {:answer/id #uuid "3f6f6e35-54ed-5c70-99bf-e9c53ec01e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331274} {:answer/id #uuid "9595bd2c-208d-534f-bec1-062cbf04a750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f6f6e35-54ed-5c70-99bf-e9c53ec01e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331274} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac11ea43-71fe-53da-a708-b61ae0cc214e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8c5a885f-c843-5c70-960e-5f13ff152326" :question/math-academy-id "q-129785" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/d3b5a9d779cddfb94e6bffc73c273dcc6df997259e09aed0c1b2db7c9529bc4e.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x+{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∬}_{D}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,3]\\times [-2,2]$\n- ${∬}_{R}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,4]\\times [-3,3]$\n- ${∬}_{D}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,4]\\times [-3,3]$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x+{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ad76e6b-acef-5221-8852-71dc42625bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Correct Function Used to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92931347-0953-5c8a-b2d0-c2f2a8b8f4ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331278} {:answer/id #uuid "c3113fba-5c16-5dd7-a613-35be2b9d49b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331279} {:answer/id #uuid "e4ea3495-8b7d-5f17-8db3-291ea1500446" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331280} {:answer/id #uuid "179d7cb6-d4e9-51dc-9921-a92595ffa1f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of these listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331281} {:answer/id #uuid "f30042b6-d027-598e-8daf-9f8106edd8b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f30042b6-d027-598e-8daf-9f8106edd8b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331282} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6979997-0ef2-5529-aa56-79a8a57c5a74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4630a49-9f84-56b0-b38f-98dc1ca8cec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129904" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/f8cb975b622bfe420d9418587293e83de60c297019f15e1b379bc118e079d35d.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{4}, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{4}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{4}, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/8944afb608465e49c7ae253f8e2518aa3d43b1c6e121dd91178ca1a67116a508.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{4}$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions I and III. Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(2,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function II equals $3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{4}$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ad76e6b-acef-5221-8852-71dc42625bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Correct Function Used to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29de18e0-7e63-516a-9f57-4736032f66d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331285} {:answer/id #uuid "651313b0-0b6e-5670-8f67-d5aeaf18fa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331286} {:answer/id #uuid "9795f4b9-c63c-513e-be9d-b581643b9741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331287} {:answer/id #uuid "1179ae8a-4686-5a3a-9873-42456858f5c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331288} {:answer/id #uuid "269e53e4-d737-54d0-9b71-84d5c3ebd2aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 1759