is point.\n\n- Functions II and III are equals to $x+{y}^{2}$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ad76e6b-acef-5221-8852-71dc42625bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Correct Function Used to Define a Double Integral Over a Non-Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "824efefa-195b-5945-8270-db325c41b246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151393} {:answer/id #uuid "b267ce69-f727-520e-8436-d2b61d797b6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151394} {:answer/id #uuid "ca4c22e1-3865-55ff-a6f1-9cc8c11a3fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151395} {:answer/id #uuid "0e71df1f-8709-51e6-b428-2b8b41cee33e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151396} {:answer/id #uuid "76517be8-8555-59b1-9be8-c26191bffc02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca4c22e1-3865-55ff-a6f1-9cc8c11a3fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151395} :answer-field/id #uuid "df630eba-04fb-566c-9a1a-e313478215e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ca2c9d4-83c1-5596-b062-1537df902124" :question/math-academy-id "q-80425" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/assets/d09a23a1ae9f737c7f19ba83d6d20c3fbcea3c7deb71fa307264c90afabc6580.png)